		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>While broad-coverage multilingual natural language processing tools have been developed, a significant portion of the world&apos;s over 7000 languages are still neglected. One reason is the lack of evaluation datasets that cover a diverse range of languages, particularly those that are low-resource or endangered. To address this gap, we present a large-scale text classification dataset encompassing 1504 languages many of which have otherwise limited or no annotated data. This dataset is constructed using parallel translations of the Bible. We develop relevant topics, annotate the English data through crowdsourcing and project these annotations onto other languages via aligned verses. We benchmark a range of existing multilingual models on this dataset. We make our dataset and code available to the public. 1</p>
			</abstract>
